## 🔄 **Imperative Sentences (आदेश/निवेदन)**

| Type       | Active Voice      | Passive Voice                     |
| ---------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Order      | Close the door.   | Let the door **be closed**.       |
| Request    | Please help me.   | You are **requested to help** me. |
| Suggestion | Work hard.        | You are **advised to work hard**. |
| Negative   | Don’t waste time. | Let not the time **be wasted**.   |

---

## ❓ **Interrogative Sentences (प्रश्नवाचक)**

| Type               | Active                     | Passive                           |
| ------------------ | -------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Yes/No             | Did he write a letter?     | Was a letter written by him?      |
| WH                 | Why did he write a letter? | Why was a letter written by him?  |
| Helping Verb + Sub | Is he writing a letter?    | Is a letter being written by him? |
| Modal + Verb       | Can he write a letter?     | Can a letter be written by him?   |

---

## 🗣️ **Some Voice Conversions for Practice**

| Active Voice                | Passive Voice                        |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| She sings a song.           | A song is sung by her.               |
| I will finish the work.     | The work will be finished by me.     |
| They are watching a movie.  | A movie is being watched by them.    |
| We have completed the task. | The task has been completed by us.   |
| Someone stole my phone.     | My phone was stolen. (Agent unknown) |

---

## 🧠 **Important Rules & Notes**

* हमेशा **V³ (Past Participle)** का प्रयोग Passive Voice में होता है।
* Passive में जब कर्ता ज्ञात न हो, तो **"by + agent"** हटाया जा सकता है।
* **Let + object + be + V³** का प्रयोग Imperative sentence में होता है।
* Questions में Helping Verb पहले आता है।

---

## ✅ **Uses of Passive Voice**

1. जब **कर्ता अज्ञात** हो:

   * My bag **was stolen**.
2. जब **कर्ता जरूरी नहीं हो**:

   * The road **was repaired**.
3. जब **कार्य पर जोर** देना हो, न कि करने वाले पर:

   * The Taj Mahal **was built** in 1632.

